{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else","id":975578,"title":"Do Proximi seem incredibly weak to anyone else?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-24T10:27:50-07:00","id":975578,"title":"Do Proximi seem incredibly weak to anyone else?","content":"It seems like with Willpower as a spellcasting pool, no Arcanum rating to add to a spell's Primary Factor, and Yantras to gain bonus dice, Proximi would be <i>extremely</i> ineffective at casting spells with beyond the basic factors. And with no free Reach and Paradox success completely canceling the spell, they can't compensate by Reaching into Advanced factors without having to burn a ton of Mana, and their pool maxes out at 5. I get that not having Gnosis or Wisdom has a lot of knock-on effects that just make sense (no free Reach, no free Primary Factor, fixed spellcasting dice pool, no Attainments, etc.), but some of the other restrictions seem unduly harsh to layer on top of those limitations. Granted, they <i>should</i> by all rights be ineffective spellcasters compared to Awakened, but having to spend 5 hours and half of your mana pool to cast a Potency 1 spell that only affects a single target at sensory range for a scene and still has a 1/10 chance of doing nothing seems like too much to me. <br /> <br /> I'm considering allowing them to use a single Yantra, and maybe adjusting the way Paradox affects their spells so that it warps them normally instead of cancelling them. Would such a change be game-breaking or lore-breaking in any way I'm not seeing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:33:28-07:00","id":975581,"title":"","content":"No it won't break anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:49:26-07:00","id":975597,"title":"","content":"Proximi get a free Reach to spend on Blessings as of the errata. That helps somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:21:25-07:00","id":975611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=975597#post975597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Proximi get a free Reach to spend on Blessings as of the errata. That helps somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I had forgotten that. Yeah, that helps a fair bit actually, because it frees them up from having to risk Paradox just to cast at Sensory Range, or Instant speed.<br /> <br /> Is there an in-universe reason that Paradox affects their spells differently than it does Awakened mages' spells? I understand why they can't Contain Paradox, but why does it work differently whe they release it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-24-2016, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:29:25-07:00","id":975618,"title":"","content":"Probably because the harsh version of their curse kicking in when they score a Paradox is bad enough. I think you could basically say that the Curse is a sort of &quot;safe&quot; channel that the Paradox can be sent into which is pretty handy since Proximi don't have the same resources for dealing with Abyssal threats that Mages have, but they pay for it on a very personal level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:54:02-07:00","id":975629,"title":"","content":"I always saw it as a drawback to being born partly connected to a Watchtower. It's like growing up near unshielded powerlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T14:10:18-07:00","id":975692,"title":"","content":"I agree about the effect of paradox on proximi, never been a fan. I'd personally suggest having it so when they release it it has the normal effects, but also affects their curse as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:26:41-07:00","id":975711,"title":"","content":"I find Proximi, as written, extremely lackluster. To the point that I honestly struggle to see how one is supposed to use them in game.<br /> <br /> As allies they are niche at best, assuming a fairly standard spread of 3-5 players one of the Cabal will almost certainly be better at doing anything a Proximi could. As Antagonists they are unimpressive, even the most potent possible Proximi (15+ Blessings, Willpower 10) is going to be outclassed in their familial field by a starting mage who happens to focus on those Arcana (which again, with an expected 3-5 player spread is almost guaranteed), and they aren't common enough to be a threat in numbers. I guess one could use them as a mystery jumping point, chasing the legacy of an Archmage, but without a means to study supernal symbols <s>or leap into Astral Realms</s> (right you are Mrmdubois) Proximi themselves cannot offer a whole lot on that front.<br /> <br /> They don't even share the themes of the awakened, they aren't Addicted to Mysteries, they don't struggle with Hubris, they can't study the hidden symbols that rule society. It seems to me that they fill basically the same niche as mortals with supernatural merits, which is a pity because 'cursed sorcerers, who inherit supernal power' really is splendid narrative territory.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Okay, so as not to be a total kvetch, there are two themes which I find Proximi do explore quite well: Choice &amp; Entitlement.<br /> <br /> <i>Choice </i><b>- </b>Mages, all Mages, choose to Awaken. Proximi do not, they have power and a curse thrust upon them exclusively because of who their parents (or great, great, great, etc, grandparents) are. Proximi can make the point, one most Mages would balk at, that not everyone <b>wants </b>to awaken. Some people were quite happy living an ignorant, sleepy life.<br /> <br /> <i>Entitlement </i><b>- </b>Proximi (can) also have something Mages do not: Pedigree. Agatha, a Sister of the Mountain, isn't some uppity city chick who hated her job so much she went magic-crazy (&lt;-Proximi POV) and now wants to save the trees. She's the heir to a long line of guardians going back generations. She's got history, upbringing, and a curse that keeps her in line. In other words, she has the <b>right</b> to do what she does. She pays the price, she keeps the tradition. What Mage can honestly claim to do the same? And what give them the right to intervene?<br /> <br /> These two themes are excellent, and pose questions the Awakened may otherwise never consider. Unfortunately, when push come to shove Proximi don't have the bite to backup their bark, and end up having to run to other Mages for help. Which kinda ruins it if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-24-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:38:08-07:00","id":975714,"title":"","content":"Proximi can enter the Astral on their own, that's one of the uses of Astral Adept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T22:38:42-07:00","id":975838,"title":"","content":"I use them as 'lesser' sorcerers, compared to Awakened. Remember, Orders are filled with mediums, psychics and other 'gifted', all at Status 1. At this level, Proximi are the most desired as most close to the proper Awakened - their Blessings makes them understand Arcana the most. I imagine Silver Ladder is 'Proximi biased', wanting most to have Proximi under their wings, hoping for their Awakening.<br /> <br /> But I'm still baffled by using Proximi as foot soldiers or canon folder, like <b>DaveB</b> used Myrmidons in <b>Soul Cage</b>. By the gameline descriptions, Proximi are rare - <i>really rare</i>. Using them to battle mages is waste of possible good lower agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:44:52-07:00","id":976012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=975838#post975838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm still baffled by using Proximi as foot soldiers or canon folder, like <b>DaveB</b> used Myrmidons in <b>Soul Cage</b>. By the gameline descriptions, Proximi are rare - <i>really rare</i>. Using them to battle mages is waste of possible good lower agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair the Myrmidons are sort of a special case. They're a pre-Fall race of proximi who have been dedicated to serving the General for untold eons. They have been breeding specifically to serve the General since 'time immemorial,' so presumably have had a lot of time to build up their forces.<br /> <br /> Plus, considering the events of Soul Cage it was probably considered important enough to sacrifice swathes of them.<br /> <br /> It was a bad tactical decision, especially given the method used to bring them in, but the General is basically the god of 'throw more men at them.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:42:44-07:00","id":976031,"title":"","content":"I also find them lackluster in general, im thinking of just going the quickroute of 1st edition personally.<br /> <br /> Transform a spell with merit dot. Proximi can use said spell. No paradox no family curse, to me it seems the closest to Ascension`s Sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:13:22-07:00","id":976381,"title":"","content":"Proximi better resemble the Fae Touched from the (not as of yet) released second edition of Changeling: The Lost. They have a reduced fuel-pool compared to their full-splat counterparts, nor inherantly have access to the same benefits or privileges, nor even a gradual access to the same level of power their bretheren. They are between a normal human and a proper Mage/Changeling, with some of the benefits but also the downsides with some unique to themselves.<br /> <br /> The question I have is how Proximi compare to other minor-splats within the CoD? It's been established here that they generally don't compare very well to a Mage, even a starting one, and I'm having a hard time really finding a unique advantage to them. At least Fae-Touched serve as a bridge between Changelings and the normal world, and can find their way through the Hedge to their promised other - it makes for an effective way to direct a rescue party (though that has pitfalls beyond mere navigation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:52:54-07:00","id":976396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=976012#post976012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair the Myrmidons are sort of a special case. They're a pre-Fall race of proximi who have been dedicated to serving the General for untold eons. They have been breeding specifically to serve the General since 'time immemorial,' so presumably have had a lot of time to build up their forces.<br /> <br /> Plus, considering the events of Soul Cage it was probably considered important enough to sacrifice swathes of them.<br /> <br /> It was a bad tactical decision, especially given the method used to bring them in, but the General is basically the god of 'throw more men at them.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was thinking that Seers can MADE Myrmidons, Hollow or others from normal Sleepers. Or it was thing I was getting from <b>Seers of Throne</b> book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:30:13-07:00","id":976421,"title":"","content":"Seers &quot;make&quot; most of their servitors, but the Myrmidons are an exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:41:44-07:00","id":976513,"title":"","content":"Well, in comparison to vanilla Mortals, their powers are nice (even having access to healing, scrying, and the like is useful when otherwise impossible). In a Mage game, as PCs, they probably serve best as &quot;introductory&quot; characters - PCs start as Proximi, learn the ropes of the Awakened, before Awakening themselves.<br /> <br /> You can patch them (such as with the various Proximus focused Merits in the Homebrew thread) up to the point where they are workable. They'll never surpass a full Mage, but they aren't supposed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:51:46-07:00","id":976545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=976421#post976421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seers &quot;make&quot; most of their servitors, but the Myrmidons are an exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>So rest of servitors <i>are</i> Proximi? If yes, then Myrmidons can easily be hacked to be ones also - and that Seers then can 'mass produce' them. Then cannon folder take has much more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:56:10-07:00","id":976549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=976513#post976513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can patch them (such as with the various Proximus focused Merits in the Homebrew thread) up to the point where they are workable. They'll never surpass a full Mage, but they aren't supposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even as backup characters they sound really weak, compared to the spirits, ghosts or goetia, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:19:36-07:00","id":976560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=976513#post976513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in comparison to vanilla Mortals, their powers are nice (even having access to healing, scrying, and the like is useful when otherwise impossible). In a Mage game, as PCs, they probably serve best as &amp;quot;introductory&amp;quot; characters - PCs start as Proximi, learn the ropes of the Awakened, before Awakening themselves.<br /> <br /> You can patch them (such as with the various Proximus focused Merits in the Homebrew thread) up to the point where they are workable. They'll never surpass a full Mage, but they aren't supposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my concern was less that they wouldn't measure up to Mages (of course they won't, nor should they), and more that their limitations would leave them unable to actually do much of anything with their Gifts under the 2e casting system. Upon further investigation and trying to put together some spells for a Proximi character, I think I may have underestimated them. They're no good at casting most spells that have Potency as a primary factor, but more Duration-based spells work fine for the most part. One Reach for Instant and one Reach for Extended Duration, maybe one or two steps up the Duration chart is actually plenty for a lot of spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:11:54-07:00","id":976597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=976545#post976545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So rest of servitors <i>are</i> Proximi? If yes, then Myrmidons can easily be hacked to be ones also - and that Seers then can 'mass produce' them. Then cannon folder take has much more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, only the Myrnidons are Proximi. As was mentioned earlier though the Myrmidon are an ancient lineage, as a result there are a lot of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T23:22:30-07:00","id":977004,"title":"","content":"When I think of Proximi the first thing that comes to my mind is the oriental assistant of Dr. Strange. Yes he helped with rituals and occult knowledge, but mostly he was a highly trained combatant and bodyguard for a normally squishy Mage.<br /> \u200bI've been trying to figure out an interesting use for Proximi in my Mage chronicles, so far I've only used one as a prize they had to retrieve, maybe having them trained by the orders since childhood to fill roles and have skills new Mages never needed before Awakening, skills like sword fighting or advanced knowledge of Spirits, would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 09-27-2016, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T01:47:53-07:00","id":977071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=977004#post977004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI've been trying to figure out an interesting use for Proximi in my Mage chronicles, so far I've only used one as a prize they had to retrieve, maybe having them trained by the orders since childhood to fill roles and have skills new Mages never needed before Awakening, skills like sword fighting or advanced knowledge of Spirits, would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a worldbuilding perspective, I think Proximi, and more generally the existence of a Status 1 servant class, help Mage society make more sense and the Orders function more like they're described in the writeups and books. In a Chronicle of mine from a few years ago, there was an ongoing subplot about a cabal of apostates being held prisoner while awaiting judgment at the Consilium and the logistics of how a city of 50-60 mages (more than in Broken Diamond) could keep 24/7 tabs on three prisoners was a real head-scratcher for me. Even if you only had one guard on duty, assuming 8-hour shifts, you'd need three people pulling a shift every single day to have full coverage. Wouldn't these mages have better things to do, I wondered? Who manned the Athenaea and Lorehouses, who accompanied Sentinels and Citizen-Agents on their patrols?<br /> <br /> Finding out that the Orders are meant to be staffed with reams of Proximi and Sleepwalkers (a fact that was very well-hidden in 1e) really helped cast the setting in a new light for me, and opened up a lot of story possibilities. They help keep the wheels turning and have an immense amount of trust reposited in them, but they're human and can be co-opted, subverted, threatened, kidnapped, impersonated - or they can just turn on their employers after suffering one too many insults from some high-handed Mystagogue. At the same time, though, they aren't supernaturally compelled to pursue magic or chase down personal Obsessions, and they might form each Order's &quot;silent majority,&quot; the backbone of true believers who really do wake up every morning wanting to help recover the secrets of the Awakened city or defend mankind from supernatural threats or destroy the servants of the Lie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:30:56-07:00","id":977214,"title":"","content":"Admittedly with the Proximi I almost immediately felt that they were a bit lackluster. In order for me to fully use them, I had to actually fully rewrite their themes for them to be an enjoyable option. One of the methods I came up with was the idea that actually being a Proximi was a Mystery in itself that leads to Awakening. Give them a mage sight, give them enough correspondences to things relative to the Supernal, and give them the option of Awakening when they understand (know academically know, but understand) this Mystery fully, and you have a full viable story and goal with them. <br /> <br /> Of course, my writeup saw mixed thoughts because I buffed them up to the point where they could contend with mages even if mages were still ultimately superior (blessings were treated as rotes, which because of how rotes work seemed a bit too far to folks in the other direction) But I like it comparatively. I do admittedly like that they added the free reach, but I still don't think it helps much (because that free reach also didn't give them a free dot of spell control or any clarification on that - do they get 1 dot of spell control? None? Is it a non-issue for them?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:07:51-07:00","id":977237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=977071#post977071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a worldbuilding perspective, I think Proximi, and more generally the existence of a Status 1 servant class, help Mage society make more sense and the Orders function more like they're described in the writeups and books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gives you some justification for having been 'raised' into magic, too, so you're not a complete newbie when you start out, as well a reason for having Sleepwalker family members or loved ones.<br /> I mentioned in a post a while back that since, upon Awakening, mages aren't exactly taught about quiescence, they are likely to cause a lot of damage to people all around them unless they get picked up quick. Some people desperately want to avoid that sort of tragedy or abuse in the background of their characters so they can have their family be proximi, which not only allows them to not have their minds caved in by the magic, but can allow them to live a life that doesn't involve completely lying to whoever they supposedly care about.<br /> <br /> I'll grant that these aren't Mages-lite, and certainly don't reach the 'power level' of ghouls, but I don't think they were ever supposed to be, and the idea of rogue proximi isn't as tenable given the power and knowledge accessible to true mages. They can still be used as catspaws by other mages, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-27-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:48:56-07:00","id":977471,"title":"","content":"&quot;Proximi have 1 free Reach for casting their blessings, and add 1 die of Paradox for every additional Reach.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just read that in the changes to 2e mage thread , the doc file.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T17:11:11-07:00","id":977485,"title":"","content":"Rogue Proximi would likely seek out the support and protection of something bigger then they are if they've betrayed a Mage Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T17:25:52-07:00","id":977487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=977471#post977471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Proximi have 1 free Reach for casting their blessings, and add 1 die of Paradox for every additional Reach.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just read that in the changes to 2e mage thread , the doc file.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we established this in like the third post of the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T17:37:27-07:00","id":977493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=976396#post976396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I was thinking that Seers can MADE Myrmidons, Hollow or others from normal Sleepers. Or it was thing I was getting from <b>Seers of Throne</b> book.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were 'made' but just in an original sense. The origin ties in with Zeus and the 'actual' myrmidons, except I believe it's the General that raised an ant to become a Myrmidon. Interesting thing to note, while not quite human, Myrmidons can Awaken, and always do so as Obrimos, which makes sense as the General is the Forces Exarch.<br /> <br /> Gave me a good idea for upcoming game, really thankful you mentioned them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:46:42-07:00","id":980471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=977487#post977487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we established this in like the third post of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oops, my bad, sorry, should have payed better attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:25:44-07:00","id":981068,"title":"","content":"Making more Myrmidons is easy - breed them to other Myrmidons, as they've been doing for ages! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else#post975578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like with Willpower as a spellcasting pool, no Arcanum rating to add to a spell's Primary Factor, and Yantras to gain bonus dice, Proximi would be <i>extremely</i> ineffective at casting spells with beyond the basic factors. And with no free Reach and Paradox success completely canceling the spell, they can't compensate by Reaching into Advanced factors without having to burn a ton of Mana, and their pool maxes out at 5. I get that not having Gnosis or Wisdom has a lot of knock-on effects that just make sense (no free Reach, no free Primary Factor, fixed spellcasting dice pool, no Attainments, etc.), but some of the other restrictions seem unduly harsh to layer on top of those limitations. Granted, they <i>should</i> by all rights be ineffective spellcasters compared to Awakened, but having to spend 5 hours and half of your mana pool to cast a Potency 1 spell that only affects a single target at sensory range for a scene and still has a 1/10 chance of doing nothing seems like too much to me.<br /> <br /> I'm considering allowing them to use a single Yantra, and maybe adjusting the way Paradox affects their spells so that it warps them normally instead of cancelling them. Would such a change be game-breaking or lore-breaking in any way I'm not seeing?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact I would say them not using a Yantra would be unusual. Instrumentality is so important to magical tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:23:45-07:00","id":983621,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the already noted errata gives a nice bump to Proximi, and their place in Awakened society helps focus them as characters, I\u2019ll add in a few things.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Remember Proximi can gain and use Supernatural Merits, some of which give abilities not to sneeze at (Deadpan, for instance). If you want A Proximus to fling greater fireballs, nothing is wrong with giving her Pyrokinesis Merit. They also tend to be the head (or fairly close to) of Cults, which gives perks themselves. (Whether they gain Mystery Cult Influence, I am sketchy on).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, the idea to allow Proximi to use a Yantra to modify their spells does clash with the in-world logic of what Yantras are: ways of focusing a Mage\u2019s Imago through their understanding of the Truth\u2019s of the World (i.e. Gnosis). As Proximi don\u2019t have Gnosis, they can\u2019t use Yantras. Buuuut, a way of shifting the wording gives me an idea.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permutation: It\u2019s in the Blood</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While a Proximus does not have the Gnosis to channel Yantras for her Blessings - since she is does not have the understanding of Truth in the world- she does have a Magical connection: Herself. She is born of magic, and she can tap into that birthright to achieve greater results with her Blessings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: When casting a Blessing, if the Proximus engages semiotics related to his Oblations, he gains a +1 equipment modifier to his Blessing roll. If he engages in a ritual, he can gain an extra +1 modifier by using another Oblation effect.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Finally, if he spends a point of Willpower, he can gain +5 bonus dice instead of +3 if he works in his Curse into the Blessing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: The Proximus is still limited by the same Yantra cap as mages, and if he works his Curse into his Blessing, the Persistent Curse worsens, slightly. A Sister of The Mountain gains an Resistant Bashing or Lethal Wound, or her Life Plant drains some of her life essense, and she gains a Deprived Condtion, and needs to eat or gain some other Nutrients.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2377-wyrm-sage","name":"Wyrm Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2377_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:23:39-07:00","id":985844,"title":"","content":"Interesting, but it might be simplier maybe for Mages to create magic items that function as Yantras that use they're creators Gnosis somehow. Not sure if that's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:20:55-07:00","id":989690,"title":"","content":"If I was going to give proximi a weakness when mages don't have a weakness I'd at least make them immune to quiescence as long as they don't exceed their reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10831-bauran","name":"Bauran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10831_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:32:29-07:00","id":989791,"title":"","content":"I think one big advantage Proximi have when hanging around with Mages is that they get access to appropriately-aspected Supernal Verges and Demesnes. They can cast spells just fine in those. <br /> <br /> Also they can use Imbued items a lot more easily than regular sleepwalkers. No need to visit a Mage to get it recharged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T05:29:20-07:00","id":989831,"title":"","content":"Honestly, after reading the official version I kinda prefer the ones in PenDragon\u00b4s homebrew, both thematically and in regarding firepower. No offense to the writting team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:14:44-07:00","id":989909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975578-do-proximi-seem-incredibly-weak-to-anyone-else?p=976549#post976549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even as backup characters they sound really weak, compared to the spirits, ghosts or goetia, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to remember as a trade-off for being modestly less potent than a spirit is that proximi are also human. It may not come up much if your ST would rather just leave your followers under your absolute control, but your retainers being human in mindset, having human connections, human ambitions... Those are a tremendous advantage. Your Mage gets not only a potent ally who can see them as they are, but one who can be a friend and empathize with them.<br /> <br /> In terms of raw power, proximi may sit lower on the spectrum, but they're still people with whom you can find understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}